  {
    "id" : "angular_no-service-method",
    "level" : "Info",
    "category" : "BestPractice",
    "subCategory" : null,
    "title" : "Enforce use of factory() instead of service() in AngularJS",
    "description" : "This rule enforces the use of the factory() method instead of service() when defining AngularJS services.",
    "explanation" : "<!-- WARNING: Generated documentation. Edit docs and examples in the rule and examples file ('rules/no-service-method.js', 'examples/no-service-method.js'). -->\n\n# no-service-method - use `factory()` instead of `service()`\n\nYou should prefer the factory() method instead of service()\n\n**Rule based on Angular 1.x**\n\n**Styleguide Reference**\n\n* [y040 by johnpapa - Services - Singletons](https://github.com/johnpapa/angular-styleguide/blob/master/a1/README.md#style-y040)\n\n## Examples\n\nThe following patterns are considered problems;\n\n    /*eslint angular/no-service-method: 2*/\n\n    // invalid\n    angular.module('myModule').service('myService', function() {\n        // ...\n    }); // error: You should prefer the factory() method instead of service()\n\nThe following patterns are **not** considered problems;\n\n    /*eslint angular/no-service-method: 2*/\n\n    // valid\n    angular.module('myModule').factory('myService', function () {\n        // ...\n    });\n\n    // valid\n    angular.module('myModule').value('someValue', {\n        // ...\n    });\n\n## Version\n\nThis rule was introduced in eslint-plugin-angular 0.1.0\n\n## Links\n\n* [Rule source](/rules/no-service-method.js)\n* [Example source](/examples/no-service-method.js)",
    "enabled" : false,
    "timeToFix" : 5,
    "parameters" : [
