    "id" : "regexp_no-empty-capturing-group",
    "level" : "Warning",
    "category" : "ErrorProne",
    "subCategory" : null,
    "title" : "Disallow Empty Capturing Groups in Regular Expressions",
    "description" : "This rule disallows the use of capturing groups in regular expressions that capture empty content, such as those capturing assertions.",
    "explanation" : "---\npageClass: \"rule-details\"\nsidebarDepth: 0\ntitle: \"regexp/no-empty-capturing-group\"\ndescription: \"disallow capturing group that captures empty.\"\nsince: \"v0.12.0\"\n---\n# regexp/no-empty-capturing-group\n\n💼 This rule is enabled in the ✅ `plugin:regexp/recommended` config.\n\n<!-- end auto-generated rule header -->\n\n> disallow capturing group that captures empty.\n\n## :book: Rule Details\n\nThis rule reports capturing group that captures assertions.\n\n<eslint-code-block>\n\n```js\n/* eslint regexp/no-empty-capturing-group: \"error\" */\n\n/* ✓ GOOD */\nvar foo = /(a)/;\nvar foo = /a(?:\\b)/;\nvar foo = /a(?:$)/;\nvar foo = /(?:^)a/;\nvar foo = /(?:^|b)a/;\n\n/* ✗ BAD */\nvar foo = /a(\\b)/;\nvar foo = /a($)/;\nvar foo = /(^)a/;\n```\n\n</eslint-code-block>\n\n## :wrench: Options\n\nNothing.\n\n## :rocket: Version\n\nThis rule was introduced in eslint-plugin-regexp v0.12.0\n\n## :mag: Implementation\n\n- [Rule source](https://github.com/ota-meshi/eslint-plugin-regexp/blob/master/lib/rules/no-empty-capturing-group.ts)\n- [Test source](https://github.com/ota-meshi/eslint-plugin-regexp/blob/master/tests/lib/rules/no-empty-capturing-group.ts)",
