    "subCategory" : null,
    "title" : "Enforce Brace Style",
    "description" : "Enforce consistent brace style for blocks including TypeScript-specific constructs such as enum, interface, namespace, and module declarations.",
    "explanation" : "---\ndescription: 'Enforce consistent brace style for blocks.'\n---\n\n> 🛑 This file is source code, not the primary documentation location! 🛑\n>\n> See **https://typescript-eslint.io/rules/brace-style** for documentation.\n\nThis rule extends the base [`eslint/brace-style`](https://eslint.org/docs/rules/brace-style) rule.\nIt adds support for `enum`, `interface`, `namespace` and `module` declarations.",
