    "id" : "vue_require-render-return",
    "level" : "High",
    "category" : "ErrorProne",
    "subCategory" : null,
    "title" : "Enforce Vue Render Function to Always Return a Value",
    "description" : "This rule enforces that Vue component render functions always return a value.",
    "explanation" : "---\npageClass: rule-details\nsidebarDepth: 0\ntitle: vue/require-render-return\ndescription: enforce render function to always return value\nsince: v3.10.0\n---\n# vue/require-render-return\n\n> enforce render function to always return value\n\n- :gear: This rule is included in all of `\"plugin:vue/vue3-essential\"`, `\"plugin:vue/essential\"`, `\"plugin:vue/vue3-strongly-recommended\"`, `\"plugin:vue/strongly-recommended\"`, `\"plugin:vue/vue3-recommended\"` and `\"plugin:vue/recommended\"`.\n\n## :book: Rule Details\n\nThis rule aims to enforce render function to always return value\n\n<eslint-code-block :rules=\"{'vue/require-render-return': ['error']}\">\n\n```vue\n<script>\nexport default {\n  /* ✓ GOOD */\n  render (h) {\n    return h('div', 'hello')\n  }\n}\n</script>\n```\n\n</eslint-code-block>\n\n<eslint-code-block :rules=\"{'vue/require-render-return': ['error']}\">\n\n```vue\n<script>\nexport default {\n  /* ✗ BAD */\n  render (h) {\n    if (foo) {\n      return h('div', 'hello')\n    }\n  }\n}\n</script>\n```\n\n</eslint-code-block>\n\n## :wrench: Options\n\nNothing.\n\n## :books: Further Reading\n\n- [Guide - Render Functions](https://vuejs.org/guide/extras/render-function.html)\n\n## :rocket: Version\n\nThis rule was introduced in eslint-plugin-vue v3.10.0\n\n## :mag: Implementation\n\n- [Rule source](https://github.com/vuejs/eslint-plugin-vue/blob/master/lib/rules/require-render-return.js)\n- [Test source](https://github.com/vuejs/eslint-plugin-vue/blob/master/tests/lib/rules/require-render-return.js)",
