  {
    "id" : "vue_valid-define-props",
    "level" : "High",
    "category" : "ErrorProne",
    "subCategory" : null,
    "title" : "Enforce Valid defineProps Compiler Macro",
    "description" : "This rule enforces the correct usage of the Vue 3 `defineProps` compiler macro to ensure props are defined properly and consistently.",
    "explanation" : "---\npageClass: rule-details\nsidebarDepth: 0\ntitle: vue/valid-define-props\ndescription: enforce valid `defineProps` compiler macro\nsince: v7.13.0\n---\n# vue/valid-define-props\n\n> enforce valid `defineProps` compiler macro\n\n- :gear: This rule is included in all of `\"plugin:vue/vue3-essential\"`, `\"plugin:vue/essential\"`, `\"plugin:vue/vue3-strongly-recommended\"`, `\"plugin:vue/strongly-recommended\"`, `\"plugin:vue/vue3-recommended\"` and `\"plugin:vue/recommended\"`.\n\nThis rule checks whether `defineProps` compiler macro is valid.\n\n## :book: Rule Details\n\nThis rule reports `defineProps` compiler macros in the following cases:\n\n- `defineProps` is referencing locally declared variables.\n- `defineProps` has both a literal type and an argument. e.g. `defineProps<{/*props*/}>({/*props*/})`\n- `defineProps` has been called multiple times.\n- Props are defined in both `defineProps` and `export default {}`.\n- Props are not defined in either `defineProps` or `export default {}`.\n\n<eslint-code-block :rules=\"{'vue/valid-define-props': ['error']}\">\n\n```vue\n<script setup>\n/* ✓ GOOD */\ndefineProps({ msg: String })\n</script>\n```\n\n</eslint-code-block>\n\n<eslint-code-block :rules=\"{'vue/valid-define-props': ['error']}\">\n\n```vue\n<script setup>\n/* ✓ GOOD */\ndefineProps(['msg'])\n</script>\n```\n\n</eslint-code-block>\n\n<eslint-code-block :rules=\"{'vue/valid-define-props': ['error']}\">\n\n```vue\n<script setup lang=\"ts\">\n/* ✓ GOOD */\ndefineProps<{ msg?: string }>()\n</script>\n```\n\n</eslint-code-block>\n\n<eslint-code-block :rules=\"{'vue/valid-define-props': ['error']}\">\n\n```vue\n<script>\nconst def = { msg: String }\n</script>\n<script setup>\n/* ✓ GOOD */\ndefineProps(def)\n</script>\n```\n\n</eslint-code-block>\n\n<eslint-code-block :rules=\"{'vue/valid-define-props': ['error']}\">\n\n```vue\n<script setup>\n/* ✗ BAD */\nconst def = { msg: String }\ndefineProps(def)\n</script>\n```\n\n</eslint-code-block>\n\n<eslint-code-block :rules=\"{'vue/valid-define-props': ['error']}\">\n\n```vue\n<script setup lang=\"ts\">\n/* ✗ BAD */\ndefineProps<{ msg?: string }>({ msg: String })\n</script>\n```\n\n</eslint-code-block>\n\n<eslint-code-block :rules=\"{'vue/valid-define-props': ['error']}\">\n\n```vue\n<script setup>\n/* ✗ BAD */\ndefineProps({ msg: String })\ndefineProps({ count: Number })\n</script>\n```\n\n</eslint-code-block>\n\n<eslint-code-block :rules=\"{'vue/valid-define-props': ['error']}\">\n\n```vue\n<script>\nexport default {\n  props: { msg: String }\n}\n</script>\n<script setup>\n/* ✗ BAD */\ndefineProps({ count: Number })\n</script>\n```\n\n</eslint-code-block>\n\n<eslint-code-block :rules=\"{'vue/valid-define-props': ['error']}\">\n\n```vue\n<script setup>\n/* ✗ BAD */\ndefineProps()\n</script>\n```\n\n</eslint-code-block>\n\n## :wrench: Options\n\nNothing.\n\n## :couple: Related Rules\n\n- [vue/define-props-declaration](./define-props-declaration.md)\n- [vue/valid-define-emits](./valid-define-emits.md)\n- [vue/valid-define-options](./valid-define-options.md)\n\n## :rocket: Version\n\nThis rule was introduced in eslint-plugin-vue v7.13.0\n\n## :mag: Implementation\n\n- [Rule source](https://github.com/vuejs/eslint-plugin-vue/blob/master/lib/rules/valid-define-props.js)\n- [Test source](https://github.com/vuejs/eslint-plugin-vue/blob/master/tests/lib/rules/valid-define-props.js)",
